From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: minhmc2007 <quangminh21072010@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:47:13 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] hbm: disable, it needs ash 0.38+ but this tree has 0.37.3

error[E0433]: failed to resolve: could not find `khr` in `ash`
error[E0599]: no method named `push_next` found for struct
               `PhysicalDeviceFeatures2`
... 68 errors total

hbm's refs/heads/main is written against ash 0.38+, which has the
ash::khr and ash::ext submodules and the struct builder methods that
hbm/src/sash.rs uses. This tree, like LineageOS 23.2, provides ash
0.37.3, which has `pub mod extensions` and no builders. The Waydroid-ATV
android-crates-io fork is also 0.37.3, so swapping it in does not help
either.

The four downstream hbm modules are already enabled: false, and nothing
in device/waydroid or vendor/extra references libhbm, mapper.hbm or
hostbm, so disabling the remaining two drops hbm out of the build
instead of importing a newer ash.

This costs hbm's Vulkan/DRM host buffer manager, so a future ash 0.38+
crate is needed if that path is wanted.
---
 Android.bp | 22 ++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
index 2e7b7a7..1d61d9f 100644
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -23,6 +23,12 @@ rust_library {
     features: [
         "ash",
     ],
+    // hbm main targets ash 0.38+ (ash::khr / ash::ext modules and the struct
+    // builder methods). LineageOS 23.2 provides ash 0.37.3, which has
+    // `pub mod extensions` instead, so hbm/src/sash.rs does not compile. Nothing
+    // in the product references any hbm module, so disable it rather than import
+    // a newer ash.
+    enabled: false,
 }
 
 rust_binary {
@@ -54,6 +60,8 @@ rust_ffi_static {
         "liblibc",
         "liblog_rust",
     ],
+    // see the comment on libhbm above; also needs ash 0.38+
+    enabled: false,
 }
 
 rust_ffi_static {
@@ -76,15 +84,13 @@ cc_library_shared {
     vendor: true,
     shared_libs: ["liblog"],
     export_include_dirs: ["hbm-minigbm/include"],
+    // The arch block this used to carry re-enabled the module on x86 and
+    // x86_64, which overrode the enabled: false above and left it depending on
+    // the now-disabled libhbm_minigbm_rust:
+    //   error: module "libhbm_minigbm" variant "android_vendor_x86_64_shared":
+    //     depends on disabled module "libhbm_minigbm_rust"
+    // Removed so the module actually stays disabled.
     enabled: false,
-    arch: {
-        x86: {
-            enabled: true,
-        },
-        x86_64: {
-            enabled: true,
-        },
-    }
 }
 
 cc_library_shared {
